--
-- Test Description
-- This test checks the operation of the RX TCP offload engine, with IP frames
-- with SNAP and ethernet encapsulation, which have good IP checksum and are
-- valid TCP or UDP frames with good checksums
-- This test is run in gigabit TBI FIFO mode.
-- 
-- Functional Coverage
-- * Checks that the TOE recognises that these are TCP or UDP frames
--   and therefore checks the TCP/UDP checksum.
-- * Checks that the TOE can correctly compute TCP and UDP checksums for both 
--   odd and even length frames.
-- * Checks that the GEM can correctly report different types of encapsulation
--   and IP frames.
-- 
-- Detailed Test Description
--  1. Initialise suitable wait states for the test.
--  2. Check reset values of registers and setup interrupts
--     and then enable receive in TBI mode into a 32-bit FIFO data bus.
--  3. Send several IP frames with either SNAP or ethernet encapsulation, which
--     have good IP checksum and are valid TCP or UDP with good checksums.
--
-- Test 2.1
--    Broadcast frame, Valid TCP, even length, no IP options, no VLAN, no SNAP
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums checked (bits [23:22] = 10) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 2.2
--    Broadcast frame, Valid TCP, odd length, IP options, no VLAN or SNAP
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums checked (bits [23:22] = 10) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 2.3
--    Broadcast frame, Valid TCP, Max length IP options, IP header 60 bytes,
--    VLAN, no SNAP.
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums checked (bits [23:22] = 10) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 2.4
--    Broadcast frame, Valid UDP, odd length, no IP options, no VLAN, no SNAP
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & UDP
--    checksums checked (bits [23:22] = 11) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 2.5
--    Broadcast frame, UDP null checksum, VLAN, SNAP (checksum is last data)
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & UDP
--    checksums checked (bits [23:22] = 11) and SNAP (bit 24 high).
-- Test 2.6
--    Broadcast frame, Valid IP + TCP (no VLAN, no SNAP), Max length (1518
--    octets including CRC)
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums checked (bits [23:22] = 10) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 2.7
--    Broadcast frame, Valid IP + TCP (no VLAN, with SNAP, type/length = 0x5DC)
--    Long packet, consistent with type/length = 0x5DC.
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums checked (bits [23:22] = 10) and SNAP (bit 24 high).
-- Test 2.8
--    Broadcast frame, UDP null checksum, VLAN, SNAP (checksum is not last data)
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & UDP
--    checksums checked (bits [23:22] = 11) and SNAP (bit 24 high).
-- Test 2.9
--    Broadcast frame, UDP null checksum, VLAN, SNAP, zero UDP length.
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & UDP
--    checksums checked (bits [23:22] = 11) and SNAP (bit 24 high).
-- Test 2.10
--    Broadcast frame, Valid TCP, even length, no IP options, no VLAN, no SNAP.
--    TCP sequence number field is 32'h00000000, which corresponds to NULL
--    UDP checksum value. Test ensures NULL UDP is ignored.
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums checked (bits [23:22] = 10) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
--
--  4. Check statistics for correct values from above tests.
--
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------


--******************************************************************************
--  1. Initialise suitable wait states for the test.
--******************************************************************************
wait_states 0
bus_grant_delay 0


--******************************************************************************
--  2. Check reset values of registers and setup interrupts
--     and then enable receive in TBI mode into a 32-bit FIFO data bus.
--******************************************************************************
-- check and initialise the relevant registers
apbrd(100) 00 00000000  -- check reset value of network control register
apbrd      04 00080000  -- check reset value of network config register
apbrd      08 00000006  -- check reset value of network status register
apbrd     200 00009040  -- check value of pcs control register
apbwr     200 00000040  -- disable autonegotioation
apbrd     200 00008040  -- check autoneg disabled
apbwr      04 01080c01  -- enable RX TCP offload engine. and TBI mode, 32 bit.
apbrd      04 01080c01  -- verify write to network config register.
apbrd      24 00000000  -- check interrupt status
apbwr      28 ffffffff  -- enable all interrupts
apbrd      24 00000000  -- check interrupt status
apbwr      00 00000004  -- enable receive

apbrd(int) 24 00000200  -- check link status change interrupt


--******************************************************************************
--  3. Send several IP frames with either SNAP or ethernet encapsulation, which
--     have good IP checksum and are valid TCP or UDP with good checksums.
--******************************************************************************


